{#
  Renders a track's "Practice set" section from content/{track}/_practice-set.json — a flat,
  numbered list of free-response problems (course_schema.json #/definitions/practiceSet), distinct
  from bank-data/*.json's MCQ pools and from chapter blocks[] content. Two real variants exist
  (WP17 audit, appc) — see course_schema.json's practiceSet definition for the full account of why
  they differ; each renders its own real toggle/DOM shape, existing engine.js JS is unmodified
  either way.

  The intro <p> and heading are real per-track copy — a WP12 audit found this partial had been
  hardcoding qudrat's own wording (mentioning "quantitative comparisons", a qudrat-only question
  type) for every track, live and wrong on the already-shipped tahsili page.

  Expects: sectionId (the section's real id, e.g. 'qud-practice' — NOT derived from trackId; must
  match the rail's data-target and any existing URL-hash deep links exactly, see rail.njk),
  practiceSet (the parsed _practice-set.json object)

  Bilingual note: item.question/item.solution are real {en,ar} fields in the schema (and in
  Qudrat/Tahsili's data as of the practice-set translation pass) but this partial previously
  rendered `.en` unconditionally — a real template gap, not a content gap: the toggle silently
  had no effect on this section even where Arabic data existed. Fixed via the standard bl.text()
  macro, same as every other block partial. item.solution uses tag='div' since its content
  contains block-level <p> tags (bl.text()'s own doc comment: use a block tag when the field's
  HTML itself has block content). practiceSet.introText is a plain string, not a {en,ar} field —
  no schema for that yet, left as-is (a separate, larger change: would need adding it across all
  21 tracks' _practice-set.json, not just this template).
#}
{% import "partials/_bilingual.njk" as bl %}
{% set LVL_CLASS = {"Basic": "b", "Intermediate": "i", "Advanced": "a"} %}
<section class="chapter" id="{{ sectionId }}">
  <div class="chead"><span class="cn">{{ practiceSet.icon or '§' }}</span><h2>{{ practiceSet.heading or 'Practice set' }}</h2></div>
  {% if practiceSet.introText %}<p>{{ practiceSet.introText }}</p>{% endif %}

  {% if practiceSet.variant == 'compact' %}
    {% for item in practiceSet.items %}
    <div class="problem"{% if item.id %} id="{{ item.id }}"{% endif %}>
      <div class="prow"><span class="pn">{{ item.number }}</span><span class="lvl">{{ item.difficulty }}</span>
        <p class="qt">{{ bl.text(item.question) }}</p>
      </div>
      <button class="sol-toggle" onclick="this.closest('.problem').classList.toggle('open')"><span class="tw">▸</span> Show solution</button>
      <div class="solution">{{ bl.text(item.solution, 'div') }}</div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  {% else %}
    {% for item in practiceSet.items %}
    <div class="problem">
      <div class="ph">
        <span class="pn">{{ item.number }}</span>
        <p class="pq">{{ bl.text(item.question) }}</p>
        <span class="lvl {{ LVL_CLASS[item.difficulty] }}">{{ item.levelLabel or item.difficulty }}</span>
      </div>
      <button class="sol-toggle" onclick="toggleSol(this)"><span class="tw">▸</span> Show solution</button>
      <div class="solution">{{ bl.text(item.solution, 'div') }}</div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  {% endif %}
</section>
